After installing Ubuntu, I began using the Linux Terminal, a command-line tool that allows direct interaction with the operating system. Through basic commands like ls and pwd, I learned how to navigate the file system, manage files, and understand system structure.

The Terminal is a core DevOps skill, as it enables efficient system management, automation, and troubleshooting. This work focuses on building confidence with the command line and understanding how Linux systems are controlled in real-world environments.
